Subject: realtek: l3: on-link neighbour host entries and default-route offload (RTL930x, #59)

Applied after 300-10 on the files-6.18 copy (pinned 53ec2d0). Same change against openwrt main
e5ec5e199f: upstream PR draft, docs/ROUTING-OFFLOAD.md. Both opt-in: HW routing bypasses firewall/NAT.
- l3_onlink (module param, 0644): resolved neighbour reached on-link through a switch port (kernel
  FIB lookup: unicast main route, no gateway, out of that device, shorter than /32 or /128) gets a
  host-table entry forwarding to its MAC. v4 and v6 (v6 host hash = SDK hostHash0/1, checked by
  scripts/l3_hash6_check.py; host slots tracked in a bitmap since a 3-slot v6 entry reads back
  only at its first slot). Torn down on neighbour invalid/dead, move to another link, a FIB route
  taking the address, or a covering route change that makes it ineligible; no free slot -> none
  (on-link prefix trap row takes it). Link-local v6 never.
- l3_default_v4, l3_default_v6 (module params, 0644; per family so v6 can forward while v4 stays
  off on a NAT box, #58): 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 via a gateway gets a row above the catch-all
  (place() keeps the catch-all last); forwards only while no route of the family lacks an entry (hw_missing on the list, or lost[] for one that could not even be listed; cleared by a
  FIB replay, requested on the next delete). A v6 source-specific default traps the row.
- Poll every DELAY_PROBE_TIME: entry hit + neighbour STALE -> neigh_event_send() (kernel re-probes,
  as mlxsw); next hops still without an L2 entry retried; parameter changes applied.
- linux-next: ARP table per netns, arp_table(&init_net) (7.3 copy: openwrt/patches-v7.3-rc6/).
